\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A direction selected by the faces}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Each face of a [slab](fdip-01AE) distinguishes one
normal projector. At an interior layer the two projected
components come from different neighbors. The coefficients of
the transverse Wilson operator determine whether these inputs
specify a unique step. When does advancing in this direction
give a strictly positive self-adjoint operator?}
